      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_lUa46N3WdbKweXHYak-idvdjLHm9jYc0P4IiAI9BlAGU2U=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Israel, I have deep memories that have lasted for 40 years.  \n\nI served with UNDOF in 1987 and experienced the majesty at the center of humanity for 7 months.  Our camp was on the Golan Heights and we took our mission seriously, but I was a sponge when it came to learning history.  I saw the country from North to South, East to West.  \nAcre, Netanya, Caesarea, the Negev, Eilat, Masada, the Dead Sea, Jerusalem, Bethlehem, the Via Dolorosa, the Western Wall, Tel,Aviv… I saw it all! \nI’m so grateful to have been able to walk the ground in historic locations and to have left my mark on history, including floating ON, not IN the Dead Sea 😉\n\nI came to love the country and its people and unlike the prejudiced media, I embraced Jews, Christians, Arabs  alike.  I have missed Israel but cherish my memories.  I miss hummus and falafel the most. \n\nSwimming in Lake Tiberius was always a favourite; as was St Peter’s fish.  \n\nI saw the ugly ( I remember, but prefer not to discuss), and I saw the resilience of the Israeli population.  It’s important to understand that Israel is comprised of Christians, Arabs and Jews.  \nIsrael welcomes all, is a refuge for Jews and is a very welcoming country.  I’m happy to have been a temporary citizen from Canada for 7 months in 1987.  \n\nThe food, the culture, the absolute acceptance by Israelis and the resolve to endure, no matter the cost.  ❤️",
